1972. First and Last Call On the Same Day
Table: Calls
Column Name	Type
caller_id	int
callee_id	int
call_time	datetime

There is no primary key for this table.

Each row represents a phone call made from caller_id to callee_id at call_time.

Task

Write an SQL query to report the distinct user ids of the people whose:

first call and last call on the same day were with the same person

A user can appear as either:

the caller, or

the callee

Rules & Clarifications

A call involves two users: caller_id and callee_id

A user’s first call of a day is the call with the earliest call_time on that day

A user’s last call of a day is the call with the latest call_time on that day

The other person in the first call and last call must be the same

Return each user only once

Return the result table in any order

Example
Input

Calls

caller_id	callee_id	call_time
1	2	2021-07-01 08:00:00
2	1	2021-07-01 09:00:00
1	3	2021-07-01 20:00:00
3	1	2021-07-02 10:00:00
1	3	2021-07-02 20:00:00
Output
user_id
2
3

Solution
--------
with all_calls as
(select caller_id as user1, recipient_id as user2, call_time
from Calls
union all
select recipient_id, caller_id, call_time
from Calls),

first_last_calls as
(select distinct user1, 
    first_value(user2) over(partition by user1, date(call_time) order by call_time asc) as first_call,
    first_value(user2) over(partition by user1, date(call_time) order by call_time desc) as last_call
from all_calls)

select distinct user1 as user_id
from first_last_calls
where first_call = last_call

